    },
    "bytecode": "KLUv/QBYIQAAAAAAAA==",
    "text": "Begin WhyWalkRiderPin\n\nfloat px\nfloat py\nfloat pz\nfloat pa\n\nif ( whywalk_active == 0 )\n    return\nendif\n\nset px to whywalk_x\nset py to whywalk_y\nset pz to whywalk_z\nplayer->SetPos X px\nplayer->SetPos Y py\nplayer->SetPos Z pz\n\nif ( whywalk_yawdelta != 0 )\n    set pa to ( player->GetAngle Z + whywalk_yawdelta )\n    player->SetAngle Z pa\n    ; Consume on use. Lua writes a fresh delta every frame it wants one, so\n    ; zeroing here means a dropped or repeated frame cannot re-apply a turn\n    ; the mount already made.\n    set whywalk_yawdelta to 0\nendif\n\nEnd WhyWalkRiderPin"
